<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 8.825 percent at Monday's auction from 8.820 percent at the previous auction on July 28.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 1,099.350 million pounds, replace bills worth 702.375 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for one billion pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Feb 3, 1998 (Jan 27, 1998)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.825 percent (8.820)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,099.350 million (992.975 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,404.850 million (1,242.975 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.500-8.950 percent (8.450-8.994)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.500-10.200 percent (8.450-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 95  (105)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 105 (110)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
